$ {\rm Tors}_\Gamma(N) \to S_{N \rtimes \Gamma}$. The inverse maps a section $s$ to the set $P=s(\Gamma)\backslash(N \rtimes \Gamma)$ where the $\Gamma$-equivariant $N$ right torsor structure comes from right translation with $N \rtimes \Gamma$.
\end{pro}

